{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat collab/1793387762000-engineer-ts-t3-merge.codex.findings.md && rg -n \\\"T3|S10|portab|linked|cross.unit|oracle seam|pending\\\" orchestrator-logs/179*yang* 2>/dev/null | tail -100 && sed -n '1,120p' test/yang/typescript/antlr/linked_harness.cljc && sed -n '1,250p' test/yang/typescript/antlr/linked_prelude_test.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"# yang.typescript T3 merge handoff\n\nMerged `origin/master` (`63674368311318ee8bb8032bedea11c81d89fa82`) into\n`yang-ts-t3` (HEAD remains `c4644d3b9bea2765f746f684f85d459f3f706da9`).\nThe merge is staged and **uncommitted**; MERGE_HEAD remains present. No unresolved\nindex entries remain. Existing untracked collaboration files were left alone.\n\n## Conflict resolutions\n\nGit produced three blocks, all in `src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc`:\n\n1. **Function factories and ordinary calls:** retained T3's five-argument\n   `js/make-function` delegating to six-argument `js/make-function-nt`, its `:nt?`\n   flag, ordered `js/om-new` property descriptors and prototype/constructor links.\n   Added master's `:yang.call/entry` to every factory-created function cell.\n   That entry reads the original callee descriptor, refuses ordinary calls to\n   `:class`/`:derived`, preserves lexical/strict receiver handling and passes\n   `:js/undefined` as the third private-code argument when `:nt?` is true.\n   **`js/call` matches master's `yang.call/invoke-with` definition verbatim.**\n   Construction retains T3's explicit `js/construct-with-nt` path.\n2. **`js/is-constructor?`:** retained the branch definition verbatim: `:normal`,\n   `:class`, `:derived`, and `:builtin` gated by `:ctor?`.\n3. **Definition composition:** retained the complete T3 list including\n   `t4-definitions` and `class-definitions`; retained master's linked definition\n   alias and bundled/pinned shared-call runtime wiring. The branch's balanced\n   `definitions->uast` sequencing remains intact. Other files merged automatically.\n\n`test/yang/core/call_test.cljc` asserts the S0 shared descriptor/entry, invocation,\ncondition, linked/bundled emitter and original-callee identity contracts; it does\nnot assert a literal TypeScript constructor AST layout. Its S1 identity fixture\nalso survives. All four tests in that namespace were included in the quick run.\nThe original factory signature remains available, with the shared entry installed\nby the richer factory. No behavior assertions were removed or relaxed.\n\n## Validation\n\nAll test/lint commands ran in the foreground under explicit GNU `timeout` limits.\n\n- JVM quick tier: `timeout --foreground 900s clojure -M:test -e :slow -r\n  '^yang\\.typescript\\..*-test$' -n yang.core.call-test`.\n  **105 tests, 3,065 assertions; 2 failures, 0 errors.** Both failures were stale\n  address pins in `float_address_test.cljc`; all other quick checks passed.\n- The bundled prelude changes when the shared-call definitions and reconciled\n  entry are included. Updated only the two expected address constants and their\n  explanatory strings. New JVM goldens:\n  - prelude: `segment/blake3-112fda52dc1e1f0aa60e3d5fb2fedc6f6ea474567f51b63573701cb08da55f70`\n  - program: `segment/blake3-b92ab1304c794af19ef3db745dfca9a58050389029086efe54052bd989142bce`\n- Follow-up JVM run under `timeout --foreground 900s`, selecting both address tests\n  and six existing slow tests with `-v`: **8 tests, 512 assertions; 0 failures,\n  0 errors**. These exercise constructor kinds, new.target dispatch, bound\n  new.target, ordinary functions/lexical receivers/construct/escapes, shared-call\n  argument presence and shared-call foreign eligibility/identity, across all four\n  guest VMs. The program-address test also checks canonical decoding/reprojection.\n  The runtime code was unchanged between the complete quick run and this follow-up;\n  only the two stale golden tests were edited. There was no second complete quick run.\n- Kondo: `timeout --foreground 180s clj -M:kondo --lint\n  src/cljc/yang/typescript test/yang/typescript src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc\n  test/yang/core/call_test.cljc`: **0 errors, 0 warnings**.\n- `timeout --foreground 60s cljstyle check` on the resolved prelude and golden test:\n  passed. Scoped staged `git diff --check`: passed.\n- Merge-wide staged `git diff --check` flags existing whitespace in\n  `docs/design/yang.cic.md:3-4` and `docs/orchestrator-log.md:14210`; those files\n  match origin/master exactly and were not changed by this resolution.\n\nLogs: `target/t3-merge/jvm-quick.log`, `target/t3-merge/jvm-focused.log`,\n`target/t3-merge/kondo.log`. The focused log names the three test namespaces;\nits eight selected vars were constructor-kinds-test, new-target-dispatch-test,\nbound-new-target-test, shared-call-binding-presence-on-every-vm-test,\nshared-call-eligibility-on-every-vm-test, objects-and-functions-on-every-vm-test,\nprelude-address-test and program-address-test.\n\nNo unresolved semantic ambiguity remains. Node/Dart validation of the new goldens\nand the three-host verification remain with the orchestrator as requested. No\ncommit or push was performed.\norchestrator-logs/1793192500000-glm-resume-yang-clojure-hardening.md:313:Verification: engineer's counts (22/988 with 1 intentional failure; independent suites 151/2951 green); this seat's review pending.\norchestrator-logs/1793192500000-glm-resume-yang-clojure-hardening.md:366:Decisions: Rulings accepted as binding (kimi is the section-8.10 approving architect). The adoption plan + bounded engineering briefs follow, pending the coordinating owner's pinned shared runtime (A2's \"one common invocation\" and the projection helper are runtime artifacts owned by TS/PHP orchestrator).\norchestrator-logs/1793192500000-glm-resume-yang-clojure-hardening.md:387:Done: Hardening-2 round 1 delivered and verified. Gate fixtures 4->50 passes on the unchanged 54-fixture baseline (expanded corpus 53/