ntend callable-identity assertion) are the engineer's declared remaining work. The PHP half committed separately (a4b9b406) — the TS round is still in flight in the same worktree, with disjoint file ownership respected (its edits left untouched).\norchestrator-logs/1793179048-yang-php-yang-typescript-glm-resume.md:445:Done: The TS S1 round completed: the js prelude's callable constructors wired into the convention; the receiver literal-map bug fixed; the linked TS emission aligned (bundled carries helpers, linked requires the published yang.call module and pins its address). The conformance fixtures green (eligibility 1/4, lowered-source 1/56 across four VMs, linked publication 10/62, module spec 3/8, linked lowerer 1/5, S0 suites 29/500). Kondo 0/0 on 12 files. Committed 48a8e623 (the TS files only — the PHP half landed separately as a4b9b406), pushed.\norchestrator-logs/1793179048-yang-php-yang-typescript-glm-resume.md:467:Next: the yang.python orchestrator completes its integration -> the coordinated landing -> this seat continues the P4/T3/P6 tracks. The :claims scope ruling and the J6e round continue under their own seats.\n(ns yang.typescript.antlr.linked-harness\n  \"The linked profile's composition for the JavaScript tests (T1 step S5,\n   docs/design/yang.typescript.md section 13): the namespace that requires\n   this is the publisher of `js` and `jssp`, so it publishes each module\n   once per process into one in-memory content store and serves them to\n   every linked run over a `yin.vm.linker.interpreter` composition under\n   `:trusted` derivation (the remediation ruling's R6). The `:verifying`\n   evidence is `publish-module!`'s own `link-local` links, which\n   `linked-prelude-test` asserts.\n\n   A linked run builds the program's task on one of the three vector VMs\n   with a link pair, then runs the VM and serves the pair alternately\n   until the VM stops blocking, as the REPL's drive does. The AST walker\n   is not a backend here: its link of `js` is refused `:undeclared-free`\n   until L-b.\"\n  (:require [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as sr-linearize]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.derive :as derive]\n            [dao.jing.mem :as mem]\n            [yang.core.call :as call]\n            [yang.typescript.antlr.prelude :as prelude]\n            [yang.typescript.antlr.safepoint :as safepoint]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.data :as data]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn-code :as dcode]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn-register-code :as rcode]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\n            [yin.vm.integer :as integer]\n            [yin.vm.linker.interpreter :as link]\n            [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]))\n\n\n(def integer-limits\n  \"The ordinary JavaScript composition's `integer` limits.\"\n  {::integer/max-bits 100000, ::integer/max-digits 4300})\n\n\n(defn registry\n  \"The full host registry a linked JavaScript composition registers: the\n   `require` handler, then `cell`, `data`, `integer` under `limits`, and\n   `stream` — the hook module `jssp` polls a signal stream, so the\n   safepointed composition needs it even though `js` does not.\"\n  ([] (registry integer-limits))\n  ([limits]\n   (-> (module/default-registry)\n       module/register-cell-module\n       (data/register-data-module {::data/max-items 1048576})\n       (prelude/register-integer-module limits)\n       module/register-stream-module)))\n\n\n(def published\n  \"`js` published once into its own content store:\n   `{:store s :result r :address a :call-address ca}`. `yang.call` is\n   published first so `js` pins its shared calling runtime.\"\n  (delay\n    (let [store (mem/create-content-mem)\n          call-result (publish/publish-module! store (call/module-spec (registry)))\n          result (publish/publish-module! store\n                                          (prelude/module-spec (registry)\n                                                               (:address call-result)))]\n      {:store store,\n       :result result,\n       :address (:address result),\n       :call-address (:address call-result)})))\n\n\n(def published-jssp\n  \"`jssp` published once into `js`'s own content store, which its pinned\n   requirement already lives in: the same shape as `published`.\"\n  (delay\n    (let [{:keys [store address]} @published\n          result (publish/publish-module!\n                   store (safepoint/module-spec (registry) address))]\n      {:store store, :result result, :address (:address result)})))\n\n\n(defn source\n  \"The serving composition over the published store: `name-env` defaults\n   to `{js <address> yang.call <address>}`, derivation `:trusted`, the test\n   being the publisher. `jssp`-serving sources pass their own `name-env`.\"\n  ([] (source {'js (:address @published),\n               'yang.call (:call-address @published)}))\n  ([name-env]\n   (link/composition {:content-store (:store @published),\n                      :name-env name-env,\n                      :derivation :trusted})))\n\n\n(defn safepoint-source\n  \"The serving composition over the published modules: `jssp` requires\n   `js`, and `js` requires `yang.call`.\"\n  []\n  (source {'js (:address @published),\n           'jssp (:address @published-jssp),\n           'yang.call (:call-address @published)}))\n\n\n(defn publish-guest-module!\n  \"One guest module's `spec` (lower/module-spec's) published into `js`'s\n   own content store, where its pinned requirements already live:\n   `publish-module!`'s answer. Guest modules are tiny beside `js`, so a\n   test may publish its own; publish imports bottom-up, the `deps` map\n   naming each import's address.\"\n  [spec]\n  (publish/publish-module! (:store @published) spec))\n\n\n(def backends\n  \"Each vector backend's root task over a program AST and composition.\"\n  {:semantic (fn [ast opts]\n               (semantic/load-ast (semantic/create-vm opts)\n                                  (vm/ast->datoms ast)\n                                  vm/ast-contract)),\n   :stack (fn [ast opts]\n            (dvm/create-vm (:image (derive/stack-image (:vector (sr-linearize/project ast))))\n                           (assoc opts :contract vm/stack-contract))),\n(ns yang.typescript.antlr.linked-prelude-test\n  \"T1 step S5: the JavaScript runtime profile and its hook prelude as the\n   linker modules `js` and `jssp`. Both emit from the single definition\n   lists their bundled twins load; the specs declare every free name of\n   their trees; a linked run on the three vector VMs prints what the\n   bundled run prints; the AST walker's link stays refused until L-b. The\n   published modules and the linked runs are\n   `yang.typescript.antlr.linked-harness`'s: one publication per process,\n   served `:trusted`, so every test that publishes or links is slow.\"\n  (:require\n    [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n    [dao.stream :as stream]\n    [dao.test-slow :as slow]\n    [yang.safepoint :as safepoint]\n    [yang.core.uast :as u]\n    [yang.typescript.antlr.linked-harness :as h]\n    [yang.typescript.antlr.lower :as lower]\n    [yang.typescript.antlr.lower-portable-test :as portable]\n    [yang.typescript.antlr.prelude :as prelude]\n    [yang.typescript.antlr.prelude-parity-test :as parity]\n    [yang.typescript.antlr.render :as render]\n    [yang.typescript.antlr.safepoint :as hooks]\n    [yin.vm :as vm]\n    [yin.vm.data :as data]\n    [yin.vm.encoder :as encoder]\n    [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n    [yin.vm.module :as module]\n    [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]))\n\n\n(defn- refusal-of\n  \"The ex-data of what `thunk` throws, or nil when it returns.\"\n  [thunk]\n  (try (thunk)\n       nil\n       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs :default) e\n         (or (ex-data e) {}))))\n\n\n(defn- def-key\n  \"The literal key of a `(yin/def k v)` application node, else nil.\"\n  [node]\n  (when (and (map? node)\n             (= :application (:type node))\n             (= 'yin/def (get-in node [:operator :name])))\n    (get-in node [:operands 0 :value])))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The module emitters\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(deftest jssp-module-uast-is-one-wide-application-test\n  (let [ast hooks/module-uast\n        operands (:operands ast)\n        definitions (butlast operands)]\n    (is (= :application (:type ast)))\n    (is (= :lambda (:type (:operator ast))))\n    (is (= (count operands) (count (:params (:operator ast)))))\n    (is (nil? (get-in ast [:operator :body :value])))\n    (is (= (u/sexp->uast '(require (quote js)))\n           (dissoc (last operands) :tail?)))\n    (testing \"the placeholders come first, each the literal :js/uninit\"\n      (let [n (count hooks/runtime-keys)\n            placeholders (take n definitions)]\n        (is (= (mapv hooks/strip hooks/runtime-keys)\n               (mapv def-key placeholders)))\n        (is (every? #(= {:type :literal, :value :js/uninit}\n                        (dissoc (get-in % [:operands 1]) :tail?))\n                    placeholders))))\n    (testing \"then every definition, stripped, in definition order\"\n      (is (= (mapv (comp hooks/strip first) hooks/function-definitions)\n             (mapv def-key (drop (count hooks/runtime-keys) definitions)))))\n    (testing \"no symbol of the module's own namespace survives stripping\"\n      (is (not-any? (fn [x] (and (symbol? x) (= \"js.sp\" (namespace x))))\n                    (tree-seq coll? seq ast))))\n    (testing \"`js/*` references stay qualified: the base prelude's exports\"\n      (is (some (fn [x] (and (symbol? x) (= \"js\" (namespace x))))\n                (tree-seq coll? seq ast))))))\n\n\n(deftest jssp-module-exports-test\n  (is (= (set (map (comp hooks/strip first) hooks/function-definitions))\n         hooks/module-exports))\n  (is (every? #(contains? hooks/module-exports %) '[attach! loop call]))\n  (is (not-any? namespace hooks/module-exports))\n  (is (not (contains? hooks/module-exports 'cursor)))\n  (is (empty? (filter #(contains? vm/primitives %) hooks/module-exports))))\n\n\n(deftest js-module-exports-stage0-entry-points-test\n  (testing \"the lowering's literal, for-in and JSON entry points are exported\"\n    (is (every? #(contains? prelude/module-exports %)\n                '[new-object new-array literal-proto! for-in-start for-in-next\n                  install-json! define-accessor-half! json-stringify json-parse]))))\n\n\n(deftest jssp-module-spec-test\n  (let [spec (hooks/module-spec (h/registry) :test/js-address)]\n    (is (= 'jssp (:name spec) hooks/module-name))\n    (is (= hooks/module-uast (:ast spec)))\n    (is (= hooks/module-exports (:exports spec)))\n    (is (= {'js :test/js-address} (:requires spec)))\n    (testing \"a js-qualified free name is covered by the requirement\"\n      (is (empty? (filter #(= \"js\" (namespace %)) (keys (:primitives spec))))))\n    (testing \"the qualified declarations are exactly the host names\"\n      (is (= hooks/host-names\n             (set (filter namespace (keys (:primitives spec)))))))\n    (testing \"a free name no registry module supplies is refused\"\n      (let [no-cell (-> (module/empty-registry)\n                        (data/register-data-module {::data/max-items 1048576})\n                        (prelude/register-integer-module h/integer-limits))\n            refusal (refusal-of #(hooks/module-spec no-cell :test/js-address))]\n        (is (= :yang.typescript.antlr/undeclared-free\n               (:yang.typescript.antlr/refusal refusal)))))))\n\n\n(deftest js-module-spec-declares-every-free-name-test\n  (let [call-address (:call-address @h/published)\n        spec (prelude/module-spec (h/registry) call-address)]\n    (is (= 'js (:name spec)))\n    (is (= prelude/module-exports (:exports spec)))\n    (is (= {'yang.call call-address} (:requires spec)))\n    (testing \"a registry without the data module is refused\"\n      (let [no-data (-> (module/empty-registry)\n                        module/register-cell-module\n                        (prelude/register-integer-module h/integer-limits))\n            refusal (refusal-of #(prelude/module-spec no-data call-address))]\n        (is (= :yang.typescript.antlr/undeclared-free\n               (:yang.typescript.antlr/refusal refusal)))\n        (is (= \"data\" (namespace (:name refusal))))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Publication\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- publication\n  []\n  (let [{:keys [result address]} @h/published\n        links (:links result)]\n    (testing \"js publishes with no undeclared free name\"\n      (is (some? address))\n      (doseq [f [:yin.semantic/code :yin.debruijn.code :yin.debruijn.register]]\n        (is (= :ok (get-in links [f :status])) (str f))))\n    (testing \"the AST walker is refused :undeclared-free on a sibling read\n              until L-b; L-b's landing flips this assertion\"\n      (let [walker (get links :yin.ast/code)]\n        (is (= :refused (:status walker)))\n        (is (= :undeclared-free (:reason walker)))\n        (is (contains? prelude/module-exports (:name walker)))))\n    (testing \"jssp publishes over js\"\n      (let [{:keys [result]} @h/published-jssp]\n        (doseq [f [:yin.semantic/code :yin.debruijn.code :yin.debruijn.register]]\n          (is (= :ok (get-in (:links result) [f :status])) (str f)))))))\n\n\n(deftest ^:slow publication-test\n  (slow/guard \"publication-test\" publication))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Linked runs equal bundled runs\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def ^:private programs\n  \"Hand-built packets: name -> packet.\"\n  {:log-literal (portable/program (portable/log-stmt (portable/num-expr \"1\"))),\n   :var-and-log (portable/program\n                  (portable/var-stmt \"var\" \"x\" (portable/num-expr \"7\"))\n                  (portable/log-stmt (portable/name-expr \"x\"))),\n   :let-in-tdz (portable/program\n                 (portable/log-stmt (portable/name-expr \"y\"))\n                 (portable/var-stmt \"let\" \"y\" (portable/num-expr \"1\")))})\n\n\n(defn- bundled\n  [ast]\n  (render/output ((get parity/runners :semantic) ast)))\n\n\n(defn- linked\n  [k ast]\n  (render/output (vm/value (h/run-linked k ast))))\n\n\n(defn- linked-equals-bundled\n  []\n  (doseq [[nm pk] programs\n          :let [expected (bundled (lower/lower-packet pk))\n                ast (lower/lower-packet pk {:prelude :linked})]]\n    (doseq [k (keys h/backends)]\n      (is (= expected (linked k ast)) (str nm \" \" k)))))\n\n\n(deftest ^:slow linked-equals-bundled-test\n  (slow/guard \"linked-equals-bundled-test\" linked-equals-bundled))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The hook prelude linked: signals through the module boundary\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def ^:private while-loop\n  \"`while (cond) { }` over singleExpression form `cond`.\"\n  (fn [cond-form]\n    [:iterationStatement\n     [\"While\" \"while\"] [\"OpenParen\" \"(\"]\n     [:expressionSequence cond-form]\n     [\"CloseParen\" \")\"]\n     [:statement [:block [\"OpenBrace\" \"{\"] [\"CloseBrace\" \"}\"]]]]))\n\n\n(def ^:private true-expr\n  [:singleExpression [:literal [\"BooleanLiteral\" \"true\"]]])\n\n\n(def ^:private false-expr\n  [:singleExpression [:literal [\"BooleanLiteral\" \"false\"]]])\n\n\n(def ^:private spin\n  (portable/program (while-loop true-expr)))\n\n\n(def ^:private caught\n  (portable/program\n    [:tryStatement\n     [\"Try\" \"try\"]\n     [:block [\"OpenBrace\" \"{\"]\n      [:statementList [:statement (while-loop true-expr)]]\n      [\"CloseBrace\" \"}\"]]\n     [:catchProduction\n      [\"Catch\" \"catch\"] [\"OpenParen\" \"(\"]\n      [:identifier [\"Identifier\" \"e\"]]\n      [\"CloseParen\" \")\"]\n      [:block [\"OpenBrace\" \"{\"]\n       [:statementList [:statement (portable/log-stmt (portable/num-expr \"9\"))]]\n       [\"CloseBrace\" \"}\"]]]]))\n\n\n(def ^:private spin-then-log\n  (portable/program (while-loop false-expr)\n                    (portable/log-stmt (portable/num-expr \"5\"))))\n\n\n(defn- envelope\n  [pk]\n  (let [[_ [[port e]]] (lower/lower-transform {:prelude :linked} pk)]\n    (assert (= :program port))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n \"class_units|cross.unit|lower-unit|unit-a|unit-b|linked.*unit|Error subclass|Error\" test/yang/typescript/antlr src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr collab/plan-t3-v2.md'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n \"class_units|cross.unit|lower-unit|unit-a|unit-b|linked.*unit|Error subclass|Error\" test/yang/typescript/antlr src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr collab/plan-t3-v2.md'","aggregated_output":"collab/plan-t3-v2.md:140:This uses v1’s already specified operation instead of introducing the review’s alternative name `js/private-in?`. Evaluate the right operand once. A non-object right operand raises `TypeError`; an undeclared private name is an early error.\ncollab/plan-t3-v2.md:184:2. After successful parent construction, verify that `this-cell` still contains `:js/tdz`; otherwise raise `ReferenceError`.\ncollab/plan-t3-v2.md:311:**S4 — Implement `instanceof`, the Error family, and built-in subclassing**\ncollab/plan-t3-v2.md:313:Implement OrdinaryHasInstance with bound-target delegation and the required error cases. Make the Error family and supported `Object`/`Array` constructors new-target-aware.\ncollab/plan-t3-v2.md:315:Retain v1’s declared boundaries: deferred `Symbol.hasInstance`, absent stack/captureStackTrace support, plain-array results without species support, wrapper limitations, and deferred `AggregateError`. Expected divergences must have explicit fixtures and ledger references.\ncollab/plan-t3-v2.md:317:**Gate:** G0 on the instanceof matrix, Error call/construct behavior, message/cause descriptors, subclass prototype chains, and Array exotic allocation. Measure initialization cost on all four evaluators.\ncollab/plan-t3-v2.md:351:**S9 — Verify linked publication and cross-unit acceptance**\ncollab/plan-t3-v2.md:353:Factor the `lower-unit` body seam without changing existing complete-program contracts.\ncollab/plan-t3-v2.md:355:Run two separately parsed and lowered units in one task: unit A publishes its Error subclass and throwing function through `globalThis`; unit B catches the instance and checks its identity against that class, `Error`, and an unrelated sibling. Initialize once and shut down once.\ncollab/plan-t3-v2.md:359:**Gate:** G0 on linked publication and `class_units_test`; no undeclared free names; linked and bundled class results agree. Acceptance passes on four bundled and three linked evaluators. A single-unit substitute is not authorized.\ncollab/plan-t3-v2.md:363:Run every applicable `.cljc` namespace changed since S5 on JVM, Node, and Dart, including portable lowering, linked prelude, and cross-unit fixtures.\ncollab/plan-t3-v2.md:365:**Gate:** G1; Node discovery is evidenced; packet-based hosts agree on canonical output, site marks, and cross-unit behavior. Golden drift must be explained.\ncollab/plan-t3-v2.md:373:**Gate:** G2 across three hosts. Every supported entry equals pinned Node output or its recorded departure. Cross-unit Error acceptance passes; no T3 entry remains pending; all F1–F8 regressions pass. Report counts and mismatches per corpus, profile, and host.\nsrc/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/safepoint.cljc:17:   throws the guest value `js.sp/interrupt` builds (an Error object named\nsrc/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/safepoint.cljc:22:   There is no depth accounting in T1: JavaScript has no RecursionError by\nsrc/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/safepoint.cljc:78:     ;; the value an interrupt throws: an Error named Interrupt, built from\nsrc/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/safepoint.cljc:79:     ;; the exported intrinsics (the error prototype is `Error.prototype`)\nsrc/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/safepoint.cljc:82:                 (js/get-prop (js/global-get {:js/str \"Error\"})\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/cst_test.clj:260:             (cst/parse-source ts-worker [:unit 0] \"throw\\nnew Error()\"))))))\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/corpus_test.cljc:253:    (testing \"the cross-unit programs are recorded under the pinned Node\"\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/object_e2e_test.clj:36:     [(e2e/prints \"TypeError\")\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/object_e2e_test.clj:50:     [(e2e/prints \"TypeError\")\ntest/yang/ty