nfixed. S7 did not need it, because the new `capture!` covers the arrow cases.\ncollab/1793387762000-engineer-ts-t3-merge.prompt.md:7:Merge origin/master into branch yang-ts-t3 (the T3 engineering: S3-S10 + T4). The branch carries 14 commits of T3 work; master carries the landed yang.call S1 TS wiring plus the parallel seats' work. The merge has exactly three conflicts, all in src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc.\ncollab/1793387762000-engineer-ts-t3-merge.codex.findings.md:24:   `t4-definitions` and `class-definitions`; retained master's linked definition\ncollab/1793387762000-engineer-ts-t3-merge.codex.findings.md:29:condition, linked/bundled emitter and original-callee identity contracts; it does\ncollab/1793387762000-engineer-ts-t3-merge.codex.findings.md:30:not assert a literal TypeScript constructor AST layout. Its S1 identity fixture\ncollab/plan-t3-v2.md:37:- Replace v1’s S0–S7 schedule with S0–S12 below. Preserve oracle-first recording, staged activation, portability checkpoints, and independent implementation review.\ncollab/plan-t3-v2.md:68:Gate: parser regeneration succeeds; empty and nonempty static blocks produce that CST rule; existing class and T0 fixtures remain green.\ncollab/plan-t3-v2.md:251:S1 covers those cases with separately identified grammar fixtures and manifest replacements. Existing T2 oracle outputs remain unchanged; newly resolved pending entries receive their missing recorded artifacts and activation evidence.\ncollab/plan-t3-v2.md:258:- **G1 — portability checkpoint:** applicable quick `.cljc` tests on JVM, Node, and Dart. Confirm Node discovery with `Testing <ns>` evidence. Source parsing remains JVM-only; Node and Dart consume packets.\ncollab/plan-t3-v2.md:261:Tests measuring about five seconds or more receive `^:slow` and, for `.cljc`, `dao.test-slow/guard`. Bundled execution covers four evaluators; linked execution covers three while L-b remains outstanding. Prelude internals remain free of safepoints.\ncollab/plan-t3-v2.