an-t3-v2.md:357:The implementation must not concatenate source. The recorded Node oracle may use the v1-documented concatenation harness, identified in its fixture provenance.\ncollab/plan-t3-v2.md:359:**Gate:** G0 on linked publication and `class_units_test`; no undeclared free names; linked and bundled class results agree. Acceptance passes on four bundled and three linked evaluators. A single-unit substitute is not authorized.\ncollab/plan-t3-v2.md:361:**S10 — Checkpoint B: complete lowering portability**\ncollab/plan-t3-v2.md:363:Run every applicable `.cljc` namespace changed since S5 on JVM, Node, and Dart, including portable lowering, linked prelude, and cross-unit fixtures.\ncollab/plan-t3-v2.md:365:**Gate:** G1; Node discovery is evidenced; packet-based hosts agree on canonical output, site marks, and cross-unit behavior. Golden drift must be explained.\ncollab/plan-t3-v2.md:369:Enable all T3 steps and resolved T2 grammar handoffs. Run separate bundled/linked corpus legs for T1, T2, and T3, plus the classes e2e fixture.\ncollab/plan-t3-v2.md:381:**Gate:** G2 evidence is complete, lint and formatting are clean, an independent non-author-family reviewer verifies the implementation, and Architect sign-off precedes the commit. The report includes exact base/landing SHAs, grammar fixtures, corpus coverage, departures, lane counts, and discovery evidence.\ncollab/plan-t3-v2.md:386:S0 → S1 → S2 → S3 → S4 → S5 → S6 → S7 → S8 → S9 → S10 → S11 → S12\ncollab/plan-t3-v2.md:389:V1’s remaining corpus requirements, allowed-path boundaries, runtime rulings, and acceptance obligations remain binding except where this amendment explicitly replaces them.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
